\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Visual data-construction workflow.} LLM-assisted programs generate voxel shapes and descriptions, followed by deduplication, voxel-to-brick tiling, repair, contact-based screening, and audited export for downstream fine-tuning. The dashed arrow denotes repair or retiling when needed. This diagram summarizes the historical construction workflow; screening is distinct from a guarantee of physical stability. Brick colors follow the type legend in Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:teaser}.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
